  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_pack_cb385f75e7af1e404cb18f1b33111959832584ce9a6e98678bb3a129275e4f3ae5">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>pack: a packing unit and measure for dry goods, flax, cloth, yarn, candlewick and similar wares — both a physical unit of transport of no particular size and, for some commodities, a measure of definite size (flax: 150 bales = 20 cwt at 112 lb./cwt; candlewick: 20 cwt; Irish yarn: 4 cwt at 120 lb./cwt; Cologne thread: 30 dozen lb.) (Zupko 270-1). See also packet, fardel, truss; for pack-thread see packthrede; for the pack-needle and packduck see those.</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
